% A customer asks a web shop to erase their personal data (GDPR Article 17).
% The shop keeps the invoices while the tax retention period runs (Article
% 17(3)(b)) and the support tickets under a litigation hold (Article
% 17(3)(e)). Marketing data goes once the customer withdraws consent for
% direct marketing (Article 21(3)). The shop tells the recipients of erased
% data about the erasure (Article 19).
% The profile and the marketing list must be erased, and the recipients of
% the marketing list must still be informed; the invoices and the tickets are
% kept, and the backup archive waits until its retention period is recorded.
% Shows exemptions as "it is not the case that", a kind of purpose, a
% decision that waits for a missing fact, and articles as quoted names.
% Source https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj (Articles 17, 19 and 21)

the templates are:
    the customer asked to erase *a record*,
    a retention period applies to *a record*,
    the retention period of *a record* has *a number* years left,
    a litigation hold covers *a record*,
    *a record* is used for *a purpose*,
    *a purpose* is a kind of *a purpose*,
    the customer withdrew consent for *a purpose*,
    *a record* was disclosed to recipients,
    the recipients of *a record* were informed,
    *a record* must be kept under *an article*,
    *a record* must be erased,
    *a record* awaits its retention period,
    the recipients of *a record* must be informed.

the knowledge base gdpr erasure includes:

% Article 17(1): personal data is erased on request, unless an exemption
% keeps it or the decision waits for its retention period.
a record must be erased
    if the customer asked to erase the record
    and it is not the case that
        the record must be kept under an article
    and it is not the case that
        the record awaits its retention period.

% Article 21(3): data for direct marketing goes once consent is withdrawn.
a record must be erased
    if the record is used for a purpose
    and the purpose is a kind of marketing
    and the customer withdrew consent for the purpose.

% Article 17(3)(b): a legal obligation to retain, here for tax.
a record must be kept under "Article 17(3)(b)"
    if the customer asked to erase the record
    and a retention period applies to the record
    and the retention period of the record has a number N years left
    and N > 0.

% Article 17(3)(e): the defence of legal claims.
a record must be kept under "Article 17(3)(e)"
    if the customer asked to erase the record
    and a litigation hold covers the record.

a record awaits its retention period
    if the customer asked to erase the record
    and a retention period applies to the record
    and it is not the case that
        the retention period of the record has a number years left.

% Article 19: the recipients of erased data are told.
the recipients of a record must be informed
    if the record must be erased
    and the record was disclosed to recipients
    and it is not the case that
        the recipients of the record were informed.

scenario erasure request is:
    the customer asked to erase the profile.
    the customer asked to erase the invoices.
    the customer asked to erase the support tickets.
    the customer asked to erase the backup archive.
    a retention period applies to the invoices.
    the retention period of the invoices has 6 years left.
    a litigation hold covers the support tickets.
    a retention period applies to the backup archive.
    the marketing list is used for direct marketing.
    direct marketing is a kind of marketing.
    the customer withdrew consent for direct marketing.
    the profile was disclosed to recipients.
    the recipients of the profile were informed.
    the marketing list was disclosed to recipients.
    erase expects answers ["the profile must be erased", "the marketing list must be erased"].
    keep expects answers ["the invoices must be kept under Article 17(3)(b)",
        "the support tickets must be kept under Article 17(3)(e)"].
    pending expects answers ["the backup archive awaits its retention period"].
    inform expects answers ["the recipients of the marketing list must be informed"].

query erase is:
    which record must be erased.

query keep is:
    which record must be kept under which article.

query pending is:
    which record awaits its retention period.

query inform is:
    the recipients of which record must be informed.
